From 09776968f925a452c5c668d70c03b52b17c1aab3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:24:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban gc: scratch archive refusals back off per
 tree; a pass budget keeps gc inside its cap

worker-2's hourly workspace GC failed two passes in a row on 2026-11-13
(`SCRATCH kanban gc board=default failed: timed out after 1800s`, receipt
ok=false, unit exit 1). Profile of the 15:02 pass (agent.log, pid 3276828):

- 15:03-15:23 aged-scratch loop: 19 trees archived and removed (~14 min),
  31 refusals (~5-6 min): partial clones whose `git bundle create` needs
  the promisor remote cost ~78 s each, other bundle failures 7-10 s,
  linked worktrees / bare repo / fifo are instant.
- 15:23-kill: gc_custody loop, ~30 removals plus more refusals (one 81 s).
- The same trees are refused on every pass (9x each in two days of logs).
- Removals are committed per tree, so the kill lost no reclaim, but it
  lost the `GC complete: N` line, so the wrapper reported the pass failed.

Five whys: the pass failed -> killed at 1800 s -> it re-pays every refusal
each hour and has no stop rule -> nothing remembers a refusal and nothing
bounds a pass -> both added here.

- New hermes_cli/kanban_scratch_backoff.py:
  * Refusals: per-tree archive refusals in
    <kanban home>/kanban/scratch-gc/refusals-<board>.json (host-local),
    backoff 2 h doubling to 24 h, forgotten after 14 days; a tree is retried
    at once when its fingerprint (path, completed_at, root inode/mtime)
    changes; a successful archive clears it; an unreadable file is empty.
  * Budget: once spent, no new archive (aged loop) or custody Board read
    starts; the rest are logged as deferred and wait for the next pass.
- gc_task_scratch archives aged trees oldest first and threads both into
  gc_custody; `hermes kanban gc --scratch-budget-seconds N` (default 1200,
  0 = no limit) leaves 600 s below the wrappers' 1800 s kill for the
  longest in-flight tree (276 s observed).

Both bounds only keep a tree for later: every ownership, custody,
owner_unverified, live-job and snapshot guard still runs for every tree
that is attempted. kanban_scratch_archive.py is untouched (PR #2354).

Tests: test_kanban_scratch_gc_backoff.py, test_kanban_scratch_custody_backoff.py
(RED without the wiring: 7 of 9 fail; GREEN 9/9), plus the 32 test files
importing the touched modules (642 passed; the two 300 s-timeout files
pass alone, 161/161).

